From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps5cemu <ps5cemu@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:28:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: the software keyboard drawn by the port, in its menus'
 language

Cemu's keyboard has English keys only: a player whose console speaks
Russian, Japanese or Thai has no way to type a name in their alphabet, a
German one no umlauts, and its labels and hints are English whatever the
language. Its font, the Wii U's own at ImGui's default glyph ranges, has
only Latin-1 besides.

On the console the port draws it instead (PS5Cemu_DrawKeyboard), as it
draws the 3DS's keyboard: over the game, in its menus' typeface, with the
language's pages of keys, which L1 and R1 go through, and its words. The
form's text goes to the port as UTF-16 and comes back as typed, to at
most the length swkbd_keyInput allows, within the form; a change is
written back and reported as a key's is, and the port's OK or Options
finishes the input as Enter did. The game showing the keyboard again
(SwkbdAppearInputForm, SwkbdAppearKeyboard) starts the port's over.

The port's earlier changes to Cemu's keyboard (its size at 4K, the
D-pad's focus, Triangle as shift, the English hints) go: the port reads
the DualSense for its own keyboard. Elsewhere nothing changes.
